` is never invoked**, so a NULL `op` is harmless |","-| E24 | `process_with_foreach` | `arr->count < 0` — `FOREACH` terminates on `count_iter != size`, which is never true for negative `size` | runs away past the array (undefined / crashes). Not differentially testable; both implementations perform the identical address arithmetic. |","-| E25 | `process_with_foreach` | `op` is NULL **and** `arr->count > 0` | calls through a NULL function pointer → SIGSEGV in both (verified out-of-process) |","-| E26 | `process_with_foreach` | `op` returns an extreme value (e.g. `INT32_MAX`) so `result * 0.75` needs clamping | `item->value` saturates via `safe_double_to_int` |","-| E27 | `compute_weighted_sum` | `arr->count <= 0` | loop never runs; returns `0` |","-| E28 | `compute_weighted_sum` | `i == 0` — `current > base` is false, so the pointer-difference weight would be `0` | falls back to `weight = 1` (**not** 0) |","-| E29 | `compute_weighted_sum` | `current->value * weight * 0.8` exceeds int range | each term saturates via `safe_double_to_int`; `sum` accumulates with wraparound |","-| E30 | `arrayfunc` | `param3 * 2` overflows `int` (e.g. `param3 = INT32_MAX`) | two's-complement wraparound (`-O0` gcc), no trap |","-| E31 | `arrayfunc` | `param1 + param2` / `param2 - param3` overflow `int` | two's-complement wraparound |","-| E32 | `arrayfunc` | `param4 == INT32_MIN` → `param4 / 2` (divisor is the constant `2`, so `INT_MIN / -1` cannot occur) | `-1073741824`, then `+1` → `-1073741823` |","-| E33 | `arrayfunc` | accumulated `result` overflows `int` before the final `* 0.333` | wraparound, then the final `safe_double_to_int` clamp |","-| E34 | *any of* `compare_results_in_array`, `init_result_array`, `process_with_foreach`, `compute_weighted_sum` | `arr == NULL` → unconditional `arr->count` dereference | SIGSEGV in both (verified out-of-process) |","-| E35 | `init_result_array` | `values == NULL` with `count > 0` | SIGSEGV in both (verified out-of-process) |","-| E36 | `operati