{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_xz6owxr5c77iecu24qibtixagq65puqhkvtmx5yj3dam6n4esfma","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. All four phases pass, and I found and fixed **three real divergences** in the Rust.\n\n## Completion gate\n\n| gate | status |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` — `nm -D` shows 0 missing / 0 undefined non-libc symbols | **PASS** (11/11, diff empty in both profiles) |\n| Phase B — every `CONFIGS.md` row passes across randomized inputs | **PASS** (33/33) |\n| Phase C — every `ERRORS.md` row has a passing error-path test | **PASS** (36/36) |\n| Holds under every feature combination | **PASS** (6 configs = 3 feature selections × 2 profiles, 84 tests each) |\n\n## Bugs found and fixed\n\n**1. `modulo_operation(INT32_MIN, -1)` — wrong termination behaviour.** The C compiles `a % b` to a single `idivl`; the implicit quotient `2147483648` doesn't fit in `eax`, so the CPU raises `#DE` and the process dies with **SIGFPE** (I measured exit 136 on the real C `.so`). The Rust used `wrapping_rem`, which silently returned `0`. Neither native Rust operator matches (`%` panics → SIGABRT under `panic=\"abort\"`; `wrapping_rem` returns 0), so I emit the actual `cdq; idiv` sequence. Both now exit with signal 8.\n\n**2. `process_with_foreach(arr, NULL)` with `count == 0`.** The C never dereferences `op` when the loop body doesn't run, so it safely returns `0`. The Rust hoisted `op.unwrap_unchecked()` *above* the loop — UB, and an abort under rustc's UB instrumentation. Now resolved inside the loop via a transmuted raw pointer, so a NULL `op` with `count > 0` also faults with SIGSEGV like the C rather than SIGABRT.\n\n**3. `compute_weighted_sum` — `offset_from` out of bounds.** A caller can hand-write `count` past the 10-element capacity; `offset_from` then violates its safety contract. Replaced with numerically identical index arithmetic, and base pointers now use `arr.cast::<Result>()` so provenance spans the whole struct.\n\n## Two judgement calls worth flagging\n\n- **Row E24 is not signal-deterministic.** The negative-`count` runaway kills the process, but repeated runs show *both* implementations producing SIGSEGV on some runs and SIGABRT on others — including a run where the C aborted and the Rust segfaulted. Asserting signal equality there would assert a coin flip, so that test asserts neither returns normally, and the *substance* (identical out-of-bounds address arithmetic and writes) is verified deterministically on a 5000-element mapped buffer with a large positive `count`.\n- **Signal-parity probes use the release `.so`.** A debug cdylib carries rustc's UB instrumentation, which turns a null deref into `abort()` before the hardware fault; CMake builds the C with nothing comparable. All defined-behaviour comparisons run against both profiles.\n\n## Why I trust the \"all green\" result\n\nPassing tests prove nothing if they can't fail, so I mutation-tested the suite itself (`./mutation_check.sh`): **40 injected bugs, all 40 caught.** Five further mutations survived — I verified each is *provably* behaviour-preserving (e.g. `>= INT_MAX` → `> INT_MAX` only changes the path for `d == 2147483647.0`, and both paths return `INT32_MAX`) and the script now asserts these *must* survive, so no survivor is left unexplained.\n\n`./run_all.sh` reproduces everything; `VERIFICATION.md` is the written report. Nothing in `c_src/` was modified (only `c_src/build/` output)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":666,"cache_read_input_tokens":239445,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":666,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c3dce5c-23e4-468e-a43a-b7c663b97536","uuid":"e984df54-3164-479d-86fc-176df52d1c18","timestamp":"2026-08-27T22:40:30.581Z"}
