e. All defined-behaviour comparisons run against both profiles.\n\n## Why I trust the \"all green\" result\n\nPassing tests prove nothing if they can't fail, so I mutation-tested the suite itself (`./mutation_check.sh`): **40 injected bugs, all 40 caught.** Five further mutations survived — I verified each is *provably* behaviour-preserving (e.g. `>= INT_MAX` → `> INT_MAX` only changes the path for `d == 2147483647.0`, and both paths return `INT32_MAX`) and the script now asserts these *must* survive, so no survivor is left unexplained.\n\n`./run_all.sh` reproduces everything; `VERIFICATION.md` is the written report. Nothing in `c_src/` was modified (only `c_src/build/` output).","ttft_ms":2519,"ttft_stream_ms":2352,"time_to_request_ms":39,"type":"result","duration_ms":2911036,"uuid":"55c8c035-bd96-4506-a718-b2a35e4bf948","queued_turn_count":0}
